Tom Cat wrote:
>
> I'm just a simple Orc Wizard on this quest to find the Amulet of
> Yendor.  I only get down to level 4 when my Chaotic Orc nature gets the
> best of me and I decide to make sure I kill every monster on the level.

Every monster including friendlies?  If you kill all
hostiles and leave the peacefull ones that is unmixed
good.  If you also kill the peacefull ones you need to
know exactly why you are doing so and what the price
is.  Generally the alignment penalty for killing a
peacefull is several times the alignment bonus for
killing hostiles, but the ratio of friendly to hostile
is large enough to offset it.  The earlier you are in
the game the more important that alignment matters.
Then again the earlier you are in the game the more
important are the objects carried by those peacefulls.
Nethack is *wonderfull* with conundrums like that.

> Oh my where did this pack of jackles come from?!?  Well that's
> not so bad.  They're all in a corridor and I just force bolt them a
> couple of times and they're dead.
>
> Two more steps and 5 zombies come up the corridor.  WTF?!?

You have just learned something about going too deep
too fast.  The deeper you go *and* the more experienced
you get, the meaner the monsters *and* the more of them.
Some monsters are extremely strong on their own.  Balrogs
and minotaurs come to mind.  Other monsters are mean
because they come in packs.  Roths then solider ants then
eventually priests of Moloch come to mind.  Still other
monsters come in packs but are so weak you generally
don't need to care.  Grid bugs come to mind.

> Ok now I'm a little worried.

Worried has exactly one result - Up the stairs one or
even several floors.  If the level is higher than your
XP number early on, you're in trouble.

> No more Pw to force bolt them.  I retreat back to
